  "id": "COMPOUND:20687 - PROTEIN:5776",
  "verbalization": "Ginsenoside R10 is implicated in the biological activity of MIP through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Ginsenoside R10 acts as a target for VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of S-ethylcysteine zwitterion and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, all of which ultimately target MIP. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Ginsenoside R10 may influence MIP through these intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Ginsenoside R10 could modulate MIP activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a network of targets that collectively contribute to the observed effects, suggesting a complex, multi-step relationship between Ginsenoside R10 and MIP.",
